# The repo is scripts and rules. A game's logs and records stay on the player's PC; tools/newgame.py makes blank ones from templates/.
/runs/
/archive/
/knowledge/goals.md
/knowledge/goals-done.md
/knowledge/milestones.csv
/knowledge/fights.csv
/knowledge/travel.csv
*.log

# Working records of how this was built
/docs/review-*.md
/docs/first-hour-test.md
/docs/discovery/
/docs/ollama-plan.md

# Screenshots stay local: a capture can hold whatever the game shows.
*.png
!docs/**/*.png

# build output
bin/
obj/
__pycache__/
.cache/
mod/dist/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Game data exported by tools/kb.py (rebuilt per game version; not ours to redistribute)
knowledge/game/

# Repo-local Ollama: models, logs and the semantic index (rebuilt by tools; large)
.ollama/
knowledge/vectors/

# Local notes and the words publishcheck.py looks for: never published
CLAUDE.local.md
.publish-terms

# The player, world and goals of this machine (elin-setup): never published
player.md
